  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Md Irfan vs The State Of Jharkhand on 5 July, 2016 Author: A.B.Singh Bench: Anant Bijay Singh In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi B.A. No. 5648 of 2016 ..... Md. Irfan .... Versus The State of Jharkhand .. C O R A M : H O N ' B L E M R . J U S T I C E A N A N T B I J A Y S I N G H F o r t h e P e t i t i o n e r : Mrs Rashmi Kumari, Advocate For the State : A.P.P. 02/ Dated 5 July, 2016 th The petitioner has been made an accused in connection with Telaiya P.S. Case No. 182 of 2015 registered under Sections 272/273 of the Indian Penal Code and Section 16(1 B) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act.",
    "facts": "The petitioner has been made an accused in connection with Telaiya P.S. Case No. 182 of 2015 registered under Sections 272/273 of the Indian Penal Code and Section 16(1 B) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that coaccused persons namely Jageshwar Rajak, who is the President of village Education Committee and Meera Devi is coordinator of the Mata Samiti was the responsible person for the care of the food given to the children, who have been granted bail by this Court in B.A. Nos. 8408 of 2015 and 1010 of 2016, respectively. She also submits that petitioner is not named in the F.I.R. He further submits that petitioner is in custody since 4.6.2016.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that coaccused persons namely Jageshwar Rajak, who is the President of village Education Committee and Meera Devi is coordinator of the Mata Samiti was the responsible person for the care of the food given to the children, who have been granted bail by this Court in B.A. Nos. 8408 of 2015 and 1010 of 2016, respectively. She also submits that petitioner is not named in the F.I.R. He further submits that petitioner is in custody since 4.6.2016.",
